---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Diagram from "../../components/Diagram.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Sequence from "../../components/Sequence.astro";
import { page } from "../../lib/nav.ts";

const REQ = "server/src/iki_server/entities/requests.py";
const ACCESS = "server/src/iki_server/entities/access.py";
const MODELS = "server/src/iki_server/entities/models.py";
const TYPES = "plugins/requests/types";
const at = (label: string) => page(label).href;

const boxes = [
  { id: "registry", x: 20, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Registry", sub: "identities; registrars", href: at("Identity and HRIDs") },
  { id: "asking", x: 250, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Asking project", sub: "owns the request", href: at("Asking and serving") },
  { id: "intake", x: 480, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Intake", sub: "types and sources", href: at("Asking and serving") },
  { id: "service", x: 710, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Service project", sub: "serves it", href: at("Asking and serving") },
  { id: "entries", x: 20, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Entries and records", sub: "registry XOR project", href: at("Identity and HRIDs") },
  { id: "submit", x: 250, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Submit", sub: "one service, for good", strong: true, href: at("Asking and serving") },
  { id: "links", x: 480, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Project links", sub: "via_request", href: at("Sharing across projects") },
  { id: "guard", x: 710, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Side guard", sub: "iki.request_side", href: at("Asking and serving") },
  { id: "share", x: 20, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "shareable_into", sub: "one sharing check", href: at("Sharing across projects") },
  { id: "result", x: 250, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Deliverable", sub: "made in the service", href: at("Request and deliverable types") },
  { id: "release", x: 480, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Release", sub: "signed; then final", strong: true, href: at("Release and completion") },
  { id: "told", x: 710, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Audit and notices", sub: "both sides told", href: at("Release and completion") },
  { id: "complete", x: 480, y: 390, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Completion", sub: "every subject covered", href: at("Release and completion") },
  { id: "work", x: 710, y: 390, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Work items", sub: "the service's alone", href: at("Asking and serving") },
];
const edges = [
  { from: "registry", to: "asking" },
  { from: "asking", to: "submit" },
  { from: "intake", to: "service" },
  { from: "submit", to: "intake", label: "must match" },
  { from: "submit", to: "links" },
  { from: "registry", to: "entries" },
  { from: "entries", to: "submit" },
  { from: "service", to: "guard", label: "writes its fields" },
  { from: "share", to: "submit", label: "checks" },
  { from: "result", to: "release" },
  { from: "release", to: "links", label: "back to the asker" },
  { from: "release", to: "told" },
  { from: "release", to: "complete", label: "counts toward" },
  { from: "service", to: "work", via: [[922, 60], [922, 420]] as [number, number][] },
];

const H = {
  short: "What a request is",
  how: "The parts of a request, and the page for each",
  ref: "Code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "flow", label: "One request, from asking to release" },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      A request is a record in the project that asks, sent once to another project that serves it.
      Both sides write the same record: the asker its own fields, the service the fields the plugin
      gave it, and a database trigger keeps each to its side. Sending links the request and the
      records it names into the service. The service keeps its bench work in private work items and
      makes deliverables in its own project. A deliverable reaches the asking project only when it's
      released, usually by a signed state; released, it's final. The service marks the request
      delivered only once every recorded deliverable is back and every expected subject is covered.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A request is owned by the project that asks, and served by another (<Adr n="0132" />).</li>
      <li>A result leaves its service only by release (<Adr n="0149" />).</li>
      <li>A corrected result goes back for review (<Adr n="0179" />).</li>
      <li>Core facility requests return signed deliverables (<Adr n="0195" />).</li>
      <li><code>iki/requests</code> owns the request, work item and deliverable types (<Adr n="0211" />).</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <p>
      A request type is an ordinary plugin type with a <code>request:</code> block; a deliverable type
      has a <code>result:</code> block naming the request field and the released states. The core adds
      a <code>Request</code> row, the service's intake, and the links that carry records across. Each
      box links to the page that covers it.
    </p>
    <Diagram id="reqs" title="Projects, a request between them, and its released deliverable" width={940} height={470} boxes={boxes} edges={edges}>
      <div slot="registry">
        <p>Every project is in one registry; requests stay within it (<Adr n={[115, 132]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/org/models.py" sym="class Registry(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="asking">
        <p>The asking project owns the request: its Editors fill it in and send it (<Adr n="0132" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={MODELS} sym="class Request(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="intake">
        <p>A service's Admins say which request types it takes, and from whom (<Adr n="0132" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={MODELS} sym="class Intake(" />, <Path p={REQ} sym="def set_intake(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="service">
        <p>The project that serves requests. Its coordinators are told as one arrives (<Adr n="0142" />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/notifications/declared.py" sym="def sent(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="entries">
        <p>For a reference to a registry entry, the asker's own record of it is what's sent (<Adr n="0115" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={REQ} sym="def sent_records(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="submit">
        <p>Sending checks the asker, the revision, the intake and sharing, then links and audits both sides (<Adr n="0132" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={REQ} sym="def submit(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="links">
        <p>Links a request made carry <code>via_request</code>, and stay while they're needed (<Adr n="0132" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={MODELS} sym="class ProjectLink(" />, <Path p={REQ} sym="def why_kept(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="guard">
        <p>A trigger on each request type's tables refuses the other side's columns (<Adr n={[120, 132]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/entities/migrations/0015_requests.py" sym="iki_request_guard()" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="share">
        <p>One check decides what a project may use; unreleased results and work items are left out (<Adr n={[67, 149]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={ACCESS} sym="def shareable_into(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="result">
        <p>A deliverable must be made in the project the request was sent to, for a subject on the request (<Adr n={[149, 211]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={REQ} sym="def check_result(" />, <Path p={TYPES} /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="release">
        <p>A released state links the deliverable into the asking project once; after an independent review it's final (<Adr n={[149, 179]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={REQ} sym="def released(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="told">
        <p><code>request.submitted</code>, <code>request.received</code> and <code>request.result_released</code>, each in its own project (<Adr n="0142" />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/notifications/declared.py" sym="def released(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="complete">
        <p>The request's completed state needs every recorded deliverable returned and every commissioned subject covered (<Adr n={[132, 211]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={REQ} sym="def delivery_refusal(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="work">
        <p>Scheduling and notes live on work items no other project can link or reference (<Adr n="0132" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={`${TYPES}/work_item.yaml`} />, <Path p={REQ} sym="def check_work_item(" /></p>
      </div>
    </Diagram>

    <h3 id="flow">One request, from asking to release</h3>
    <Sequence
      id="flow-seq"
      title="A Regulated QC request to a sequencing core"
      width={900}
      actors={[
        { id: "asker", label: "Asking project", sub: "an Editor" },
        { id: "server", label: "Server" },
        { id: "service", label: "Core facility", sub: "coordinator, analyst, QA" },
        { id: "db", label: "Postgres" },
      ]}
      steps={[
        { id: "intake", from: "service", to: "server", label: "Admin: intake takes QC requests from the asker" },
        { id: "create", from: "asker", to: "server", label: "create the request, naming a tube" },
        { id: "submit", from: "asker", to: "server", label: "POST /entities/{ref}/submit" },
        { id: "link", from: "server", to: "db", label: "Request row; links into the service, via_request" },
        { id: "receive", from: "service", to: "server", label: "receipt: scan the tube in, put it away" },
        { id: "work", from: "service", to: "server", label: "accept, assign, in progress: service fields only" },
        { id: "deliver", from: "service", to: "server", label: "deliverable: submitted, reviewed, signed" },
        { id: "release", from: "service", to: "server", label: "QA signs Released" },
        { id: "back", from: "server", to: "db", label: "link the deliverable back; released_review_revision" },
        { id: "complete", from: "service", to: "server", label: "status Delivered: every tube covered" },
        { id: "read", from: "asker", to: "server", label: "GET /entities/{ref}/request: results, receipts" },
      ]}
    >
      <div slot="intake"><p>Until the intake accepts the type, sending fails with the same 404 whether the service exists or not.</p><p><Path p={REQ} sym="def not_a_service(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="create"><p>An unsent request is the asker's alone; its service fields keep their defaults.</p><p><Path p={`${TYPES}/qc_request.yaml`} />, <Path p={`${TYPES}/request.yaml`} /></p></div>
      <div slot="submit"><p>A request goes to one service, for good. A stale revision gets 412, as any write does.</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/requests.py" /></p></div>
      <div slot="link"><p>Only the records the request's <code>sends</code> fields name are linked; another of the asker's tubes isn't.</p><p><Path p={REQ} sym="def _link(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="receive"><p>The core's coordinators receive the tubes against the request: <PageLink to="Receipts and counts" />.</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/storage/receipts.py" /></p></div>
      <div slot="work"><p>The server writes as the service side inside a savepoint; the database refuses anything else.</p><p><Path p={REQ} sym="def writing(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="deliver"><p>The deliverable's states decide who signs, and keep the reviewer from releasing what they reviewed (<Adr n={[125, 128, 195]} />).</p><p><Path p={`${TYPES}/qc_deliverable.yaml`} /></p></div>
      <div slot="release"><p>The signed document names the reviewed revision when the type needs a review before release (<Adr n="0179" />).</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/signatures/services.py" sym='document["reviewed"] = reference' /></p></div>
      <div slot="back"><p>Linked into the asking project for this request, audited, and its watchers told.</p><p><Path p={REQ} sym="def released(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="complete"><p>Refused while a tube has no returned result or a recorded deliverable isn't back.</p><p><Path p={REQ} sym="def delivery_refusal(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="read"><p>The receipts are read from the <code>request.result_released</code> audit events, not a table of their own.</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/requests.py" sym="class ResultReleaseOut(" /></p></div>
    </Sequence>

    <p>Where each part is covered:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><PageLink to="Asking and serving" />: intake, sending, the two sides, work items and the queue.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Request and deliverable types" />: the <code>request:</code> and <code>result:</code> blocks, and the Plain, Research and QC pairs.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Release and completion" />: release, what's final after it, and when a request is delivered.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Sharing across projects" />: what each project can read, and why a record is held back.</li>
      <li><PageLink to="Identity and HRIDs" />: registries, entries and the project records a request sends.</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={REQ} />: intake, sending, the two sides, release and completion</li>
        <li><Path p="plugins/requests" />: the shipped request, work item and deliverable types</li>
        <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/requests.py" />: the request routes</li>
        <li><Path p="web/app/src/requests.ts" />: the app's request queries</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0132" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0142" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0149" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0179" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0195" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0211" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
